---
import { site } from '../../lib/site';
---

{
  /* ============================================================
    FOOTER CONTRACT — read before changing layout.
    History: this footer has been redesigned several times in
    ways that broke either the desktop dvh budget or the mobile
    empty-middle. The rules below are load-bearing.

    HEIGHT
      ALWAYS EXACTLY 1dvh, every viewport, no exceptions. The
      footer is the immersive close — taking the full viewport
      is the entire point. `h-dvh` on <footer> + the flex-1
      centering region + a meta row pinned to the bottom is
      what holds the budget.
        • Do NOT switch to md:h-dvh / min-h-dvh / h-screen.
        • Do NOT add py-* that pushes total content past 1dvh.
        • Do NOT "fix" empty mobile middle by removing h-dvh.
          If the middle reads as empty on a narrow viewport,
          fill it with content (show the mission band there,
          enlarge the wordmark, etc.) — never by shrinking the
          footer.

    STRUCTURE (three siblings inside <footer>, in order)
      1. orange stripe (.reveal-stripe)
      2. flex-1 wrapper with `justify-center` — holds the nav
         grid and the mission band, centered vertically in the
         remaining space.
      3. meta row (border-t) — attribution / sitemap / source.

      The meta row is OUTSIDE the flex-1 wrapper on purpose. Do
      not merge them. Do not switch the flex-1 wrapper to
      `justify-between` — it pins the mission band to the
      bottom and opens a visible gap on desktop.

    META ROW ITEMS
      Each link is wrapped in its own grid-cell <div> with
      `md:text-{left,center,right}`. The inline <a> shrinks to
      text width so :focus-visible outlines hug the link text,
      not the full 33% column. Do not unwrap.

    LINK STYLING
      One style everywhere: `nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent`.
      `.nav-link` provides the scaleX underline reveal. Do not
      introduce a second link style; the consistency is the point.

    WORDMARK SIZING
      `text-[clamp(2.5rem,7vw,4.5rem)]` — ONE fluid clamp, no
      breakpoint modifier. The wordmark is the brand's loudest
      gesture: bold, visionary, takes up space. It must only grow
      with viewport; it must never shrink.
        • 40px floor on small phones (substantial at 360px)
        • ramps through ~54px around the md transition where the
          row goes from stacked to inline-with-columns
        • caps at 72px (4.5rem) on wide desktops — same ceiling as
          the original display-md, so "for Better Transit" fits
          inside col-span-7 at the 1280px container max.
      DO NOT reintroduce a `md:` size modifier (e.g. text-display-lg
      md:text-display-md). A discrete step DOWN at the breakpoint
      contradicts "bold throughout" and has been explicitly rejected
      by the owner. Tune via the clamp's floor or vw coefficient.

    MISSION BAND
      Gated twice: `hidden md:block` AND a `max-height: 650px`
      media rule in the <style> block that hides it on short
      viewports so the footer can stay under 1dvh on small
      laptops. Keep both gates.

      No eyebrow label. The mission band is the footer's closing
      pitch, not a labelled section — the border-top + whitespace
      above already frame it. DO NOT reintroduce a "§ The work" /
      "Mission" / pilcrow-prefixed label; those read as AI template.

      Copy is evergreen. No session dates, no year references, no
      "before the 2027 Nevada session …". The why-now timeline
      lives on /why-now; the chrome ships on every page and must
      not date itself.

    ATTRIBUTION
      "Website made with love by Willie Chalmers III" links to
      https://williecubed.me. This is creator attribution, not
      site or org metadata. Do not replace with "A nonprofit
      in …" or similar.

    MOTION
      translateY + opacity only. No `scale()` transforms in the
      footer — they read as low-effort AI motion. The site's
      vocabulary is depth + opacity, not scale.
    ============================================================ */
}
<footer class="relative z-[60] bg-ink text-paper h-dvh flex flex-col">
  {
    /* Named for the View Transitions API. Latent until @view-transition
      enables cross-document transitions in global.css — harmless as a
      bare property until then. */
  }
  <div class="reveal-stripe h-2 bg-accent [view-transition-name:footer-stripe]"></div>

  {
    /* Footer is locked to exactly one dynamic viewport height (h-dvh on
      <footer>) — not a pixel taller. Stripe at top, meta row at bottom,
      and this flex-1 region centers the wordmark/link grid/mission band
      between them. overflow-hidden so any overflow on small viewports
      clips rather than stretching the footer past 1dvh. */
  }
  <div class="flex-1 flex flex-col justify-center w-full overflow-hidden">
    <div
      class="reveal-stagger container-page w-full pt-12 pb-10 md:py-[clamp(2.5rem,5vh,4.5rem)] grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-12 gap-10 md:gap-12"
    >
      {
        /* ONE fluid clamp, no breakpoint switch. The wordmark only
          grows with viewport; it never shrinks. See FOOTER CONTRACT
          → WORDMARK SIZING at the top of this file. */
      }
      <div class="reveal col-span-2 md:col-span-7">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="text-[clamp(2.5rem,7vw,4.5rem)] font-extrabold tracking-tight no-underline block"
        >
          <span class="block leading-[0.9]">Las Vegans</span>
          <span class="block leading-[0.9] text-accent">for Better Transit</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal md:col-span-3">
        <p class="eyebrow text-accent-soft">Organization</p>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-base font-semibold">
          <li><a href="/about" class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">About</a></li>
          <li><a href="/projects" class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">Projects</a></li>
          <li><a href="/events" class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">Events</a></li>
          <li><a href="/contact" class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">Contact</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal md:col-span-2">
        <p class="eyebrow text-accent-soft">Get involved</p>
        <ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-base font-semibold">
          <li><a href="/go" class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">Join us</a></li>
          <li>
            <a href={site.donate.url} rel="noopener" class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent"
              >Donate</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href={site.social.instagram}
              rel="noopener"
              class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">Instagram</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a
              href={site.social.linkedin}
              rel="noopener"
              class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">LinkedIn</a
            >
          </li>
          <li>
            <a href={`mailto:${site.email.general}`} class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent"
              >Email</a
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="footer-mission container-page w-full py-[clamp(2rem,5vh,4rem)] border-t border-paper/15 hidden md:block"
    >
      {
        /* No eyebrow. No "§ The work" / "Mission" / pilcrow label.
          The mission band is the footer's closing pitch, not a
          labelled section. Copy is evergreen — no session dates,
          no year references. See FOOTER CONTRACT → MISSION BAND
          at the top of this file. */
      }
      {
        /* reveal-stat gives the headline a heavier 24px-rise entrance —
          punches in with more force than the link columns above. */
      }
      <p class="reveal-stat text-headline-lg max-w-4xl">
        14th-busiest bus system in the country. <span class="text-accent">Zero miles of rail.</span> We're
        showing Las&nbsp;Vegans what better looks like.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {
    /* META row — structurally separate from the flex-centering region
      above. Each link is wrapped in its own grid-item <div> so the cell
      holds the column width and the inline <a> inside shrinks to text
      width. :focus-visible outlines therefore wrap the actual link text,
      not the full 33% column.

      text-sm text-paper/60 on ink blends to ~#9a9996 / 6.4:1 — passes
      AA for normal text. The earlier audit pass bumped this to /80 at
      text-xs, but the redesign's larger text-sm doesn't need the bump. */
  }
  <div class="footer-meta border-t border-paper/15">
    <div
      class="container-page w-full py-6 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 items-baseline gap-3 text-sm text-paper/60"
    >
      <div class="md:text-left">
        Website made with love by <a
          href="https://williecubed.me"
          rel="noopener"
          class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">Willie&nbsp;Chalmers&nbsp;III</a
        >
      </div>
      <div class="md:text-center">
        <a href="/sitemap" class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent">Sitemap</a>
      </div>
      <div class="md:text-right">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/LasVegasForTransit/website"
          rel="noopener"
          class="nav-link no-underline hover:text-accent"
        >
          Source on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<style>
  /* The mission band is only visible on viewports tall enough to fit it
     alongside the nav grid + meta row without forcing the footer past
     the viewport height. The threshold was tuned to match the natural
     height of the rest of the footer content. */
  @media (max-height: 650px) {
    .footer-mission {
      display: none !important;
    }
  }
</style>
